= Autonomous agent (artificial intelligence) — Technical =

== Autonomy as delegated control ==
Operational autonomy can be analyzed as the fraction/range of action-selection decisions delegated to the agent policy rather than supplied directly by an external controller.

Relevant dimensions include:

<pre>
decision horizon
action-space breadth
environment uncertainty
ability to replan
permission scope
human-intervention frequency
persistent state
failure recovery
</pre>

No universal scalar “autonomy score” is established across all systems.

== Closed-loop operation ==
An autonomous agent typically participates in a loop:

<pre>
observe
→ update state
→ choose action
→ execute
→ receive feedback
→ continue / stop / escalate
</pre>

The controller can be learned, planned, rule-based, or hybrid.

== Governance boundary ==
Human approval is compatible with autonomy when the agent independently controls decisions inside delegated bounds.

Technical descriptions should state those bounds instead of treating autonomy as binary.

